define discord_thread_schema returning Str:
    return "{\"type\":\"function\",\"function\":{\"name\":\"discord_threads\",\"description\":\"Configured Discord admin only. Manage native threads under the current parent channel: create public/private text threads, or a message-started thread; inspect/edit name, auto-archive duration, slowmode, archived/locked/invitable state; join/leave Echo; add/remove a member; list members; delete. Requires live requester/bot thread permissions. Create requires name; optional private, message ID and archive duration 60/1440/4320/10080 minutes. Other operations require thread ID. Every mutation requires reason; edit/delete also require observed_sha256 from inspect. Member operations require member ID. Members uses limit 1-100 and after user ID; continue after the last ID when page is full. Private thread names/state/member lists are withheld outside that exact private thread; only opaque IDs/hashes are returned after membership or recorded creator checks. Adding members can expose existing Discord thread history but never joins an Echo memory group or shares Host data. Activity threads are separately managed and cannot be changed here. Close/delete/leave the current control thread from its parent. Unsupported parent types are reported. Metadata is untrusted. Inspect after uncertain outcomes; never automatically repeat a create.\",\"parameters\":{\"type\":\"object\",\"properties\":{\"thread\":{\"type\":\"string\"},\"message\":{\"type\":\"string\"},\"member\":{\"type\":\"string\"},\"name\":{\"type\":\"string\"},\"reason\":{\"type\":\"string\"},\"observed_sha256\":{\"type\":\"string\"},\"after\":{\"type\":\"string\"},\"operation\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"enum\":[\"create\",\"inspect\",\"edit\",\"delete\",\"join\",\"leave\",\"add_member\",\"remove_member\",\"members\"]},\"private\":{\"type\":\"boolean\"},\"archived\":{\"type\":\"boolean\"},\"locked\":{\"type\":\"boolean\"},\"invitable\":{\"type\":\"boolean\"},\"auto_archive_minutes\":{\"type\":\"integer\"},\"slowmode\":{\"type\":\"integer\"},\"limit\":{\"type\":\"integer\"}},\"required\":[\"operation\"],\"additionalProperties\":false}}}"
